  "body": "Stacked on #1131 → #560 → #551. Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n- **`assets/posts/sinker-iso.cps`** (\"Sinker EDM (ISO)\", `posting::SINKER_POSTS`): a generic ISO-style sinker post. It writes only the RS-274 words itself (G0 with changed axis words, G90, the setup's work offset, `( )` comments). Every EDM-specific code comes from the machine's `edm.codes` (#290 D5): `metric` / `inch` (the unit word), `pickup` (`{tool}`), `reference` (`{offset}`, the electrode's pickup offset), `condition` (`{id}`), `depth` (the servo burn, `{z}`, optional `{f}`) and `end`. A stated orbit uses the machine's `edm.orbits[].word` (`{radius}`). **A missing code refuses the post by name** (\"... states no edm.codes.depth ... - fill it from the control's manual\"). A placeholder the post does not fill, or one with no value, is refused the same way. The burn posts as rapid approach, the `depth` code, rapid retract; a feed with X/Y travel, a feed up, an arc, a cycle, compensation, an rpm or a coolant ask is refused by name.\n- **`edm.codes` in the machine file** (`crates/post/src/machine/edm_codes.rs`): role -> non-empty template string; a garbled value refuses the file by its role. The mirror (and the raw CLI door, through the same parser) now carries a wire/sinker machine's `kind` and `edm` section into the script; every other machine's mirror is byte-identical.\n- **The serves law, in the engine** (`crates/post/src/post/machine_edm.rs`, called before `onOpen`): a script declares `serves = \"sinker_edm\";`. On a wire or sinker EDM, a script that does not declare that kind is refused by name before it runs, so every mill, lathe and plasma post stays refused on a sinker (and wire) EDM. A script that declares kinds is refused on any other machine, so the sinker post is refused on a mill. It holds for the app, the CLI and user `.cps` files alike. `post_serves` lists the sinker post for sinker EDMs only; `default_post_for(SinkerEdm)` is it. Wire EDM stays unserved (#533).\n- **Stream PARAMs** for a Sinker Burn (`crates/app/src/posting_edm.rs`): `EdmCondition` (the op's condition id) and `ElectrodePickup` (mm). `EdmOrbit` / `EdmOrbitRadius` are documented in `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md` and read by the post, ready for #544; nothing emits them yet.\n- **Fixture dialect** `crates/app/tests/edm/sinker-iso-dialect.mch`: SYNTHETIC invented words (`E{id}`, `M100 H{offset}`, `M101 Z{z}`, `M150 R{radius}`), not any control's.\n- Docs: `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` (the `serves` manifest key, a sinker-post section) and `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` (`edm.codes` roles). **PROCESS_VERSION 16 -> 23** (one above the highest open value, #1124's 22); it renumbers at merge.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/542-sinker-iso-post.md`. Follow-up filed: #1135 (the empty sinker template joins the built-in machine library).\n- MCP: no new command. The existing post selection and posting tools address the new registry name.\n\n## Goldens\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sinker-iso/sinker_burn_cavity.nc`: the recorded CL golden `sinker_burn_cavity.cl` posted from the post crate (the #926 direction; the CL's regeneration is pinned by app's `sinker_burn_cavity_matches_golden`).\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sinker-iso/sinker_burn_program.nc`: the real Sinker Burn op posted through `posting::post_setup` with \"Sinker EDM (ISO)\".\n\n## How tested\nPinning tests:\n- `crates/post/tests/sinker_post.rs`: `the_sinker_burn_posts_to_its_golden_against_the_fixture_dialect`, `every_missing_sinker_code_refuses_the_post_by_name` (each of metric, pickup, reference, condition, depth, end; inch; an empty section), `a_code_naming_a_placeholder_the_post_does_not_fill_refuses_by_name`, `a_stated_orbit_posts_the_machines_word_and_an_unlisted_one_refuses`, `a_mill_post_on_a_sinker_and_the_sinker_post_on_a_mill_are_refused` (fanuc, haas, tormach-plasma, fanuc-lathe on the sinker; sinker-iso on a VMC and on no machine), `a_feed_with_xy_travel_or_an_rpm_is_refused_by_name`.\n- Unit tests: `post::machine_edm::the_serves_law_reads_both_ways`, `post::machine::edm_codes::codes_read_as_words_and_garbage_refuses_by_role`.\n- `crates/app/tests/sinker_burn.rs` (through the real op): `the_sinker_burn_posts_through_the_generic_sinker_post_to_its_golden`, `a_missing_sinker_code_refuses_the_post_by_name`, `a_mill_post_on_a_sinker_machine_is_still_refused` (Fanuc, Haas, the plasma post; `post_serves` / `default_post_for`).\n- `conformance.rs`: `every_sinker_post_refuses_every_mill_golden_by_name`; the registry and extension pins list the sinker post. Every shipped post still posts every golden byte-exact.\n- Adjusted for the new registry entry: `plasma_post_refusals::the_mills_posts_decline_a_plasma_stream_and_the_1300pl` (the sinker post is refused by the serves law there), `smoothing::off_is_byte_identical_and_writes_no_smoothing_word` (skips the sinker post).\n\nGate (worktree target, sccache), head 82576ead:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green - tools, post (incl. `sinker_post`), sim, motion, app (incl. conformance, golden_cl, posting, sinker_burn, edm_machine, edm_conditions, plasma_*, smoothing), ui; 12.8 min, 0 failed. (The base includes the whole stack, so it ran broad.)\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post`: green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- **Not exercised on a real EDM control** (#290 D10). The dialect, condition and part are synthetic fixtures; a user with a real machine fills `edm.codes` from the control's manual and dry-runs before any burn.\n- No orbit is generated yet (#544), so the orbit words are pinned only from a hand-built stream.\n- No Hub run. If the Hub can simulate a sinker program, this waits on that run before it is flagged ready.\n- No library sinker machine yet (#1135).\n\nChangelog: Sinker EDM: a generic ISO-style sinker post (\"Sinker EDM (ISO)\") posts a Sinker Burn with every EDM code (unit, pickup, reference, condition, burn to depth, orbit, end) read from the machine's edm.codes; a missing code refuses the post by name, and only a post declaring it serves sinker EDM may post for one (#542)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #542\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
